      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this reject HEAD explicitly?\n\nI think `/branches/HEAD/commit` can reach this code because the branch collection exposes HEAD as a branch resource. HEAD is a symbolic ref, not an ordinary `refs/heads/...` branch. For example, it may point to  `refs/heads/master`.\n\nThat means the actual Git update may affect the target branch, while the permission checks and validators above still use `branch.branch() \u003d\u003d \"HEAD\"`.\n\nShould this mirror DeleteBranch and reject HEAD as a write target? The caller can still use the real target branch explicitly, e.g. `/branches/master/commit` or `/branches/stable-3.16/commit`.\n\nPlease also add an acceptance test for `/projects/{project}/branches/HEAD/commit`.\n\n\n```suggestion\n    if (RefNames.HEAD.equals(branch.branch())) {\n      throw new MethodNotAllowedException(\"not allowed to write to HEAD\");\n    }\n    if (RefNames.isGerritRef(branch.branch())\n        || branch.branch().startsWith(RefNames.REFS_TAGS)\n        || branch.branch().startsWith(RefNames.REFS_META)) {\n      throw new AuthException(\"not allowed to write to \" + branch.branch() + \" via this endpoint\");\n    }\n  }\n```\n\nThe suggested edit only shows the guard; it also needs the MethodNotAllowedException import and throws declaration.",
